<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marquis Zhao of Cai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 518–491 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marquis Zhao of Cai was a ruler of the Zhou state of Cai during the Spring and Autumn period. Pressed by Chu, he allied with Wu and moved his capital to Zhoulai, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shouchun">Shouxian</a> in Anhui, where he was assassinated in 491 BCE. His tomb at Shouxian yielded fine bronzes showing a refined court culture.</p></div>
